---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import "../styles/global.css";

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Restaurant",
  name: "Café Carlyle",
  servesCuisine: ["French", "American"],
  priceRange: "$$$$",
  telephone: "+1-212-744-1600",
  url: "https://www.rosewoodhotels.com/en/the-carlyle-new-york/dining/cafe-carlyle",
  address: {
    "@type": "PostalAddress",
    streetAddress: "35 E 76th St",
    addressLocality: "New York",
    addressRegion: "NY",
    postalCode: "10021",
    addressCountry: "US",
  },
  description:
    "Legendary cabaret supper club inside The Carlyle, A Rosewood Hotel — live music nightly with a two-course prix fixe dinner.",
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Café Carlyle Menu Guide — Prices & Cabaret Dining NYC"
  description="Independent guide to Café Carlyle at The Carlyle hotel: the $95 two-course prix fixe dinner, sides, desserts, cover charges, and how to plan a cabaret night. Prices reported as of October 2026."
  path="/cafe-carlyle-menu/"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
  ogImage="/images/cafe-carlyle.webp"
>
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
    <img
      src="/images/cafe-carlyle.webp"
      alt="Illustration of an intimate cabaret supper club with candlelit tables and a small stage — an artist's interpretation, not the actual Café Carlyle"
      class="w-full h-64 sm:h-96 object-cover rounded-2xl mt-8"
      fetchpriority="high"
    />

    <p class="mt-8 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-gold-dark">
      Menu Guide · Upper East Side · Cabaret
    </p>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-bold mt-2 leading-tight">
      Café Carlyle — Menu Guide
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
      Tucked inside The Carlyle at 35 East 76th Street, Café Carlyle has been the home of New
      York cabaret since 1955 — Bobby Short held court at the piano here for decades, and the
      room's Marcel Vertès murals are landmarks in their own right. Dinner runs as a two-course
      prix fixe alongside the night's performance, and the bill has two parts: the food and the
      cover charge. Below is our independent walkthrough of what the menu looks like, what it
      costs, and how to plan the evening. Everything is written in our own words; prices are
      reported figures, not a copy of the restaurant's menu.
    </p>

    <!-- At a glance -->
    <div class="mt-8 rounded-2xl border border-line bg-white p-6 sm:p-8">
      <h2 class="!mt-0 font-display text-xl font-bold">At a glance</h2>
      <dl class="mt-4 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2 text-sm">
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Location</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">35 E 76th St, New York, NY 10021 (inside The Carlyle, A Rosewood Hotel)</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Known for</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">NYC's legendary cabaret room since 1955; live music nightly</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Cuisine</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">French-leaning American supper-club fare</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Price level</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Two-course prix fixe reported at $95/person, plus a cover charge</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Hours</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Reported: Tuesday–Saturday, from 6:30 p.m.</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Reservations</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Book through Tock; check the artist calendar for cover charges</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-guide">
      <h2>The two-course prix fixe — $95</h2>
      <p>
        Dinner here is structured as a <strong>two-course prix fixe, reported at $95 per person</strong>.
        Pick one dish from the first-course list and one from the mains. The lineup is classic and
        seasonally inflected — think bistro staples executed for a room that cares as much about the
        show as the plate.
      </p>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-line my-6 not-prose">
        <table class="w-full text-sm">
          <thead>
            <tr class="bg-parchment text-left">
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">First course (pick one)</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-right">Included in prix fixe</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-line bg-white">
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Lobster bisque with Armagnac and tarragon crème fraîche</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">✓</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Baby romaine salad — soft-boiled egg, parmesan, anchovy, preserved lemon</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">✓</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Puglia burrata with baguette, apple butter, mint</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">✓</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Sunset tartare — tuna, salmon, avocado, coconut jus, shrimp chips</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">✓</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Carlyle fall salad — endive, pear, blue cheese, walnuts</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">✓</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Duck foie gras terrine with black truffle and mostarda</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">✓</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-line my-6 not-prose">
        <table class="w-full text-sm">
          <thead>
            <tr class="bg-parchment text-left">
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Main course (pick one)</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-right">Included in prix fixe</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-line bg-white">
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Faroe Island salmon with squash, zucchini, sorrel sauce</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">✓</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Branzino with charred broccoli rabe, lemon beurre blanc</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">✓</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Seafood salad — lobster, shrimp, Jonah crab, lemon vinaigrette</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">✓</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Chicken Milanese with arugula, parmesan, lemon</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">✓</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Prime porcini-crusted NY strip, potato gratin, sauce au poivre</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">✓</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Eggplant Napoleon — plant-based sausage, tofu ricotta, watercress</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">✓</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-4 py-3">Dover sole with brown butter and brioche croutons</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-right whitespace-nowrap">+$65</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>
        Our take: the Dover sole carries a steep <strong>+$65 supplement</strong> — it's the room's
        grandest gesture, but the porcini-crusted strip is the better value inside the prix fixe.
      </p>

      <h2>Sides &amp; desserts</h2>
      <p>
        Sides are extra, reported at <strong>$18 each</strong> (truffle fries at $26): creamed spinach,
        brussels sprouts with bacon and pecans, whipped potatoes, charred broccoli rabe, and grilled
        asparagus. Desserts run <strong>$24</strong> — flourless chocolate cake with raspberries, New
        York cheesecake with berries, or an apple tart with salted caramel, meringue and vanilla ice cream.
      </p>

      <h2>The cover charge</h2>
      <p>
        This is the part people miss: dinner is only half the bill. The room charges a <strong>cover
        charge reported at $80 per person and up, depending on the performing artist</strong>. Big-name
        residencies cost more; quieter weeknights less. The cover is separate from the prix fixe, and
        reservations are handled through Tock, where the current artist's terms are listed. Always check
        the calendar for your night before you book — the total per-person cost swings dramatically with
        who's on stage.
      </p>

      <h2>What we'd order</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>To start:</strong> the duck foie gras terrine — the most old-school Carlyle choice on the list.</li>
        <li><strong>The main:</strong> the porcini-crusted NY strip. Hearty enough to anchor the evening, no supplement.</li>
        <li><strong>To finish:</strong> the apple tart — salted caramel and meringue is the right kind of theater.</li>
        <li><strong>The real move:</strong> pick your night by the artist, not the menu. The room is the headliner.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Planning your visit</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Book on Tock</strong> and read the fine print for your artist's cover charge before committing.</li>
        <li><strong>Budget the full evening:</strong> $95 prix fixe + $80+ cover + drinks + tax and tip adds up fast — plan on $250+ per person for a marquee night.</li>
        <li><strong>Dress for the room.</strong> Jackets are the norm; this is one of the last places in New York where that still holds.</li>
        <li><strong>Arrive hungry but unhurried.</strong> Service is timed around the show — you're here for the whole evening, not a quick bite.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Price disclaimer -->
    <div class="mt-10 rounded-xl border border-gold/40 bg-gold/10 p-5 text-sm text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
      <p class="font-semibold text-ink mb-1">About these prices</p>
      <p>
        Prices above are <strong>reported as of October 2026</strong>, compiled from the restaurant's
        officially published menu. The prix fixe lineup, supplements, and cover charges change with
        the season and the artist — always verify current prices and the night's terms with the
        restaurant (via Tock) before visiting.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-8 text-sm text-ink-soft">
      <a href="/" class="text-gold-dark font-semibold hover:underline">← Back to all guides</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
